      "id": "get-global-context",
      "name": "GetGlobalContext",
      "category": "CoreRedirectsContext",
      "signature": "GetGlobalContext()",
      "params": [],
      "returnType": "FCoreRedirectsContext&",
      "docs": "Stores state required for FCoreRedirects API. The context encapsulates the necessary state for\nthe FCoreRedirects API to function. Changine the context can be used to change the set of\nCoreRedirects for the current thread without affecting other threads. It is up to the user to ensure\ncontexts are shared or not between threads. By default a single global context is shared amoung all\nthreads until a thread local context is set."
    },
    {
      "id": "get-thread-context",
      "name": "GetThreadContext",
      "category": "CoreRedirectsContext",
      "signature": "GetThreadContext()",
      "params": [],
      "returnType": "FCoreRedirectsContext&",
      "docs": "Returns the current context used by FCoreRedirects for the current thread. If no new context has been applied,\na global context is used for all threads."
    },
    {
      "id": "set-thread-context",
      "name": "SetThreadContext",
